<title>MEXICO: Tribasa delays share conversion.</title>
<headline>Tribasa delays share conversion.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican construction company Grupo Tribasa SA has asked its debtholders to delay a mandatory conversion of some $247.4 million in debt to shares for six months.</p>
<p>The debt should have been swapped for shares on April 21, the company said in a statement late on Monday.</p>
<p>However, the company added that debtholders who wanted to swap the debt to shares would be allowed to do so.</p>
<p>It said some 127,344,905 debt certificates had been swapped for 3,940,870 ordinary shares. It did not say how much of the total debt the certificates represented.</p>
<p>As of March, 1997, Tribasa had 141,859,264 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez Whitaker, Monterrey bureau +528 345-7617))</p>
